al movement involves summing all categories, which yields -220, indicating a net outflow from Latin America. This suggests more capital leaving the region than entering during this specific period.\n\nThe subsequent week's data (Jan 25) shows a different trend, with positive values across most categories except domestic securities. The total of 1461 represents a net inflow, reflecting a shift in capital movement compared to the previous week.\n\nI'll continue examining the table structure to ensure accurate data interpretation, focusing on the precise categorization of each financial movement.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_15b622573c854502a300849d","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"NET CAPITAL MOVEMENT\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_04.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
